{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(No_Trig_Manipulations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (No Trig Manipulations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Equilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is rotated about its center by angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57f9e462ff395eedd716f6571359abdc87dadaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\theta &lt; 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />, to form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. See the figure. The area of hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f9487813218213d012869ec3189077f042fa63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADBECF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fcaebeecca0ea8c64ba7ce4168210b4273cc739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3230e11561a7290dc4774c65dcff5e3ccd03f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d645750e37e18e0d01d20d6cf515521b8b416d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // Credit to shihan for this diagram.  defaultpen(fontsize(13)); size(200); pair O=(0,0),A=dir(225),B=dir(-15),C=dir(105),D=rotate(38.21,O)*A,E=rotate(38.21,O)*B,F=rotate(38.21,O)*C; draw(A--B--C--A,gray+0.4);draw(D--E--F--D,gray+0.4); draw(A--D--B--E--C--F--A,black+0.9); dot(O); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(A)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,dir(B)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,dir(C)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,dir(D)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,dir(E)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,dir(F)); [/asy]\" width=\"308\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/32241e9e5808498a78c248feb5289e58bb90c786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~\\frac{3}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~\\frac{4}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~\\frac{11}{13}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"429\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let O be circumcenter of the equilateral triangle \n</p><p>Easily get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47f7a6105a6da9c95d90aa5b6b72a71e3283ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OF = \\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1f78adf7c8a272d59fbfc5daa423f8630b2504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot (\\triangle(OFC) + \\triangle(OCE)) =  OF^2 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta) + OF^2 \\cdot \\sin(120 - \\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"492\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b41453814ecd3cf98cdb8982814ca7b6b0c8e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{14^2 \\cdot 3}{9} (   \\sin(\\theta)  +  \\sin(120 - \\theta) )\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18ee16322d10385622ed4077b63899a5509ae57c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{196}{3}  (   \\sin(\\theta)  +  \\sin(120 - \\theta) )\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed1d0d48b1e1a477a3d8acd54c0e3d946479122.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2 \\cdot {\\frac{1}{3}  } \\cdot(ADBECF) = 2\\cdot \\frac{91\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb39eb631f23af5984835c0887915ad764ab4e66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\theta)  +  \\sin(120 - \\theta) = \\frac{13\\sqrt{3}}{14}\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40c079b517e748fe10dadefcf3094ce60eda1f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\theta)  +   \\frac{ \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cos(  \\theta) +\\frac{ \\sqrt{1}}{2}\\sin(  \\theta) = \\frac{13\\sqrt{3}}{14}\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07240862449d49d2a1ad59ab6bbf97cdb53ee4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{3} \\sin(  \\theta) + \\cos(  \\theta) = \\frac{13 }{7}\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5444a92ee7202816473ec25e27d4d098e1f4a66f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(  \\theta)  = \\frac{13 }{7}  - \\sqrt{3} \\sin(  \\theta)\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1b4339ef8f6b42e1b65c627b2000e99c98cd4c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{169 }{49}  - \\frac{26\\sqrt{3} }{7} \\sin(  \\theta)  + 4 \\sin(  \\theta)^2 = 1\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e82a72938457ef10d65683495a21100ace7ea48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(  \\theta)  = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3} }{14}  or \\frac{4\\sqrt{3} }{7}\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba07ecb218a25398a39e54c76c6e76f897ab9fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4\\sqrt{3} }{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"43\" /> is invalid given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fde60b0c3375fed9e215ab9e67c5cd49bd10be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\leq 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065f1e5c76d7c7ee525a4023dffd6d5d64038f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\theta ) &lt; \\sin( 60^\\circ ) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} }{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\cdot 3.5}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"275\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819bb2934de4fe9499f049b4c66eec50cdf0f93f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(  \\theta)  = \\frac{11 }{14}\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974292713283938fcfb59a010823fedc894d1ff2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(  \\theta)  = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3} }{11} \\boxed{B }\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />'s side lengths of 14, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/86024fa361eb26db93952f9413ed58e530523eaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OF = OC = OE = \\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"41\" />\nWe let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc94eea7fe5b99285ed290a78bef0c2e475d38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FOC = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\nAnd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e6b8ba2444fa668812ad33d7c5ef0bc890f082.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EOC = 120 - \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b4c54efd3089c6a95c371d306b2ebd06f116f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3([\\triangle FOC] + [\\triangle COE])$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Which area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0ad6449a73b4ac1a569ea5636b091c58c79eab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle FOC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696f658779d03e046767d776812882f39390af42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)^2 \\sin(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"148\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>And area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca290a7b6aed27929f231943ef3d130ca8591fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle COE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adf8050c3e8d00f9460d01600ec57bf99fa2793a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)^2 \\sin(120 - \\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"198\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>So we have that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/537ae4f77e09dc080bed0d76adbba77f4b1bad93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)^2 (\\sin(\\theta)+\\sin(120 - \\theta)) = 91\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"377\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Which means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66aba9813c9589e761029f57d369ffaad529e7aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\theta)+\\sin(120 - \\theta) = \\frac{91\\sqrt{3}}{98}\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8133dac41978f91156dc16c780f05681d13638dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\cos(\\theta)+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{91}{98}\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/5306c73d7e87639df8f2ea3e38d96235c4839f15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\theta + 30) = \\frac{91}{98}\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d40a589fb9aeb76aed609202c4135e37dd35d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos (\\theta + 30) = \\frac{21\\sqrt{3}}{98}\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"41\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c3239eb0a37062c594ba09379192ac35ec1e3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\theta + 30) = \\frac{91}{21\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{91\\sqrt{3}}{63}\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c44768bb83598451c904bb196761ce4b1d1348f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> can be calculated using the addition identity, which gives the answer of \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf3a97fef7545196b3c3674d70b04a1e6e1ddb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\text{(B) }\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{11}}.\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>~mitsuihisashi14 \n~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a> (fixed Latex error )\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28No_Trig_Manipulations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(No_Trig_Manipulations)\">Solution 3 (No Trig Manipulations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (No Trig Manipulations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad23480cd52af6e3395c173d3b1fcad4fbaae9f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // Modified Asymptote diagram with correct right angle mark and alpha label.  import olympiad; defaultpen(fontsize(13)); size(200);  // Circumradius R = 14*sqrt(3)/3 real R = 14*sqrt(3)/3;  // Define original points with scaling pair O = (0,0); pair A = R * dir(225); pair B = R * dir(-15); pair C = R * dir(105); pair D = rotate(38.21, O) * A; pair E = rotate(38.21, O) * B; pair F = rotate(38.21, O) * C;  // Point H: Foot of altitude from B to DE pair DE_vec = E - D; pair perp_DE = (DE_vec.y, -DE_vec.x); // Rotate -90 degrees perp_DE = perp_DE / length(perp_DE); // Unit vector pair H = B - (2*sqrt(3)) * perp_DE; // Corrected direction  // Point M: Extend BH to M, BM = 13*sqrt(3)/3 pair BH_vec = H - B; pair BM_unit = BH_vec / length(BH_vec); // Unit vector along BH pair M = B + (13*sqrt(3)/3) * BM_unit; // BM = 13*sqrt(3)/3  // Point P: Midpoint of BE pair P = (B + E) / 2;  // Draw original triangles and polygon draw(A--B--C--A, gray+0.4); draw(D--E--F--D, gray+0.4); draw(A--D--B--E--C--F--A, black+0.9);  // Draw new dashed segments draw(B--H, black+0.7+dashed); draw(H--M, black+0.7+dashed); draw(O--M, black+0.7+dashed); draw(O--P, black+0.7+dashed); draw(P--E, black+0.7+dashed); draw(O--B, black+0.7+dashed);  // Draw right angle marker at OMB draw(rightanglemark(B, M, O, 15)); // Right angle at M, size 15  // Draw dots and labels dot(O); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, dir(180)); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(A)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(B)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(C)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(D)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(E)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, dir(F)); dot(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, dir(270)); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, dir(90)); dot(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, dir(0));  // Label angle POB as alpha, to the right of O draw(anglemark(B, O, P, 50)); // Angle mark at O label(&quot;$\\alpha$&quot;, O + (1.5, -.23), dir(0)); // Position to the right of O [/asy]\" width=\"308\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p>Let the circumcenter of the circle inscribing this polygon be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fedab5bc07d744eee57475d687d194df5bb11d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}*196=49\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"43\" />. The area of one of the three smaller triangles, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285efce7fabaa74905734ef9cfbc787ad09526f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DBE}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b14d789f7339bf01f389dd4a8cc43f6b5ff0a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> be the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285efce7fabaa74905734ef9cfbc787ad09526f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DBE}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, so if we extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd8f301034f6acf074d75c2d2c9367c0c82178e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MO\\perp{BM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, we get right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e867ed1eba8ff3c02e1e640e9d89cf443aae769c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{OMB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. Note that the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b029eaba3fc8ecb999778164a12be5dc5bcf165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH=2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" />, computed given the area and side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c89bc43422b9ab76c7bbe77dba4b48c8dae92a27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB=MH+HB=\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{3}+2\\sqrt{3}=\\frac{13\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"338\" height=\"43\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a79cd7d3cb09d75ad4e7725cc787b9f5a73bcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB=\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" /> so Pythag gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17ced81bc840e69db37144bbbf75f46555e51fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM=\\sqrt{OB^2-MB^2}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a49cf7d362218068d6177c5d2de31f5640b22062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HE=7-OM=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"16\" />, so Pythag gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d6a907bf750439b447c53fefe34246c0c5ea980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=2\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4b5f1b231d77db808ea15bc16c3c23c92512fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\theta}{2}=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"39\" /> and the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a58c40926be8c1444b198118bf258dd7f945528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=PE=\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" />, so that Pythag on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a615efb3534c64930413dffe84f84c9739f9257d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{OPE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710d1e83dee7dda1de00e25371a73cefb732b40c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=\\sqrt{OE^2-PE^2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{175}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"238\" height=\"45\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f45d630d688a967298dd4c5266ac4dadf760a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\alpha}=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{175}{3}}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"165\" height=\"61\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da87d1922b57a19343f1cb103b6353cac693223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{2\\alpha}=\\tan{\\theta}=\\frac{\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}}{1-\\frac{3}{25}}=\\boxed{\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"264\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>Editor's note, what happened to no trig?\n</p><p>-Magnetoninja\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdfd8eff6d97b5e254629dc4a0131cc6f541bb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle ABD] = \\frac{[ADBECF]-[\\triangle ABC]}{3} = \\frac{91\\sqrt{3}-49\\sqrt{3}}{3} = 14\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"487\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54de6bcb1d22f0d5806e74a73723138c0ac40560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DMB$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> is isosceles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6fc0a591e3aac7f45692e2df639b63fdb1af6a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMD = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30acf873c2c7457b5e1041343b31a86ccc5b6fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD = \\theta/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />. Also, all of the hexagon's internal angles are equal, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc36f0bd7226b903e00c756fe5482c7f0550b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cd5ccc669b6ab192273fdd110e3fa395df33759.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(13)); size(220);  // Base points and rotation pair O = (0,0); pair A = dir(225); pair B = dir(-15); pair D = rotate(38.21, O)*A; pair E = rotate(38.21, O)*B;  // Intersection point of AB and DE pair M = extension(A, B, D, E);  // Triangle and segments defaultpen(fontsize(13)); size(220);  // Base triangle from rotated figure pair O = (0,0); pair A = dir(225); pair B = dir(-15); pair D = rotate(38.21, O)*A; pair E = rotate(38.21, O)*B;  // M is intersection of AB and DE pair M = extension(A, B, D, E);  // Draw triangle and segment draw(A--B--D--cycle, black+0.9); draw(D--M, gray + dashed);  // Draw angle theta at AMD real r = 0.1; path thetaArc = arc(M, r, degrees(D - M), degrees(A - M)); draw(thetaArc, gray); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, M + (r+0.1)*dir((degrees(D - M) + degrees(A - M))/2), gray);  // Draw congruence ticks on MB and MD pair u1 = unit(B - M), u2 = unit(D - M); pair tick1a = midpoint(M--B) + rotate(90)*u1 * 0.04; pair tick1b = midpoint(M--B) + rotate(-90)*u1 * 0.04; pair tick2a = midpoint(M--D) + rotate(90)*u2 * 0.04; pair tick2b = midpoint(M--D) + rotate(-90)*u2 * 0.04; draw(tick1a--tick1b, gray); draw(tick2a--tick2b, gray);  // Labels dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(A)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(B)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(D)); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, N); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"172\" />\nUsing the side-angle-side area formula:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57598e17955688a6560b75fd5b9808e643a71b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14\\sqrt{3} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 14 \\cdot BD \\cdot \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) \\Rightarrow BD = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin(\\theta/2)}.\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Apply Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e195d82e3256f890a2f271bdd5cac71c963fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB = 60^\\circ - \\theta/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b72eec0c3bc50daa95e99572f9c789d99bb67888.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{14}{\\sin 120^\\circ} = \\frac{BD}{\\sin(60^\\circ - \\theta/2)}\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d53a0f15521aecee6c0d4d1d890572a3fc25591.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{28}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin(\\theta/2)\\sin(60^\\circ - \\theta/2)}.\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac770edd91db7657a34c2ed7a1516172072df0e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\theta/2)\\sin(60^\\circ - \\theta/2) = \\frac{3}{14}.\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"37\" />\nUsing trig identities:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d8cd5b9aea22d5293632f7edd0d513165b39fc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\theta)}{2}} \\cdot (\\sin(60^\\circ)\\cos(\\theta/2) - \\sin(\\theta/2)\\cos(60^\\circ)) = \\frac{3}{14}\\]\" width=\"455\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5289fb73b16297dd34394804e21a7d931e04a7f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\theta)}{2}} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cos(\\theta/2) - \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(\\theta/2)\\right) = \\frac{3}{14}\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/61558e73ff97b9ba1f75d25a427f56fa3ca58dcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\theta)}{2}} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos(\\theta)}{2}} - \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\theta)}{2}} \\right) = \\frac{3}{14}\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86aa2c1a8db0504c960927087cdf2006623bc113.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos^2(\\theta)}{4}} - \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos(\\theta)}{2}\\right)\\right) = \\frac{3}{14}\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c5b9a0af854ece483b3c6ffad14bad0a6979bc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin\\theta}{4} - \\frac{(1-\\cos\\theta)}{4} = \\frac{3}{14}\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d2710a7101e43aed3d48efb2d617246e24508c94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{3}\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\frac{13}{7}\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51f0175beff7003c092385b87f87ba13f1b95eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta = \\frac{13}{7} - \\sqrt{3}\\sin\\theta.\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Substitute into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e2874455f6b7c18b665d869dd83d047aca086a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157cea16e236d51f455f801e07584f46dd58054b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{13}{7} - \\sqrt{3}\\sin\\theta\\right)^2 + \\sin^2\\theta = 1.\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c76a8d63083f20300c95ae8a73cba92ceed4b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\sin^2\\theta - \\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{7}\\sin\\theta + \\frac{120}{49} = 0.\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Solving:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/5153e4ae8320e83b99d971af1fa75d980ab178ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\theta = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{14} \\quad (\\text{valid root}), \\quad \\cos\\theta = \\frac{11}{14} \\Rightarrow \\tan\\theta = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{11}.\\]\" width=\"435\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a58a9ca862f7a13b4fe9aca6bbb0ed0582ce641.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\text{(B) }\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{11}}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" />\n~sparkycat (ttm)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=akLlCXKtXnk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=akLlCXKtXnk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2024